  "meaningful_assertions_reviewed": [
    "Actual CliArgs parsing exercises every existing boolean/value flag and combinations; production main dispatch calls this same predicate, duplicate standalone predicate/test removed.",
    "Native expected-UID mismatch uses an actual connected Darwin Unix stream and fails with PermissionDenied before accept returns a stream. RED previously returned the unauthorized stream and failed; GREEN passes. This injects policy identity, not a real foreign account.",
    "Real private directory mode0700/owner, replacement/alias refusal, native getpeereid allow/refuse and stable startup lock lifetime are exercised; no service-under-test mocks.",
    "Occupied legacy Unix listener sees WouldBlock (no notification connection), inode unchanged and byte-identical isolated store/revision; current-session negative remains Uncertain.",
    "Regular and socket substitution after bind is refused while substitute content/mode is preserved. Failed/closed socket pathname retention is intentional, not successful race-free automatic cleanup.",
    "Thirty-two actual binds concurrent with unrelated file creations preserve baseline file modes; implementation no longer invokes umask/chmod/bootstrap. The sample supports observed behavior, not exhaustive scheduler coverage."
  ],
  "code_review_notes": [
    "accept_for_uid validates parent directory and kernel identity before publishing its local stream; error propagation drops the stream without application reads/writes.",
    "Socket0600 no longer gates bind; canonical0700 parent and type/UID/device/inode/single-link checks are retained. The code does not claim mode bits exhaust macOS ACL access. Step5 must call kernel server auth before client sends/reads bytes.",
    "No process-global permission mutation, pathname chmod or bootstrap framework remains in the reviewed channel code. No automatic unlink was introduced; lease-proven lifecycle/reclamation remains Step5.",
    "Windows names and bounded constants validate SID/store identities; allocated descriptor/native handles have owned cleanup and SAFETY context. The new decode_sid_text rejects truncation and native synchronization constant resolves in installed windows-sys source. Native Windows branches were source-reviewed, not compiled/executed on macOS.",
    "Target-only Cargo dependencies and lockfile additions reviewed: windows-sys0.60.2 for OS APIs and existing zbus5 blocking API for Linux daemon ownership query; no cloud/MCP/network listener added.",
    "Crate/super-visible new helpers have purpose/failure/ownership docs; FR anchors/deep-links retained at relevant implementing blocks. Sync doc now covers creation and rename."
